{
  "duration": 68.819,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.1,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.539,
      "end": 2.579,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.98,
      "end": 6.699,
      "text": "Now in this problem, we are given that a train is running at seventy-two kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.239,
      "end": 9.5,
      "text": "It crosses a pole in eighteen seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.92,
      "end": 12.579,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the length of the train."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.979,
      "end": 15.619,
      "text": "Now let us understand one important concept first."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.139,
      "end": 17.0,
      "text": "To cross a pole,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.459,
      "end": 20.459,
      "text": "trains travels a distance equal to its own length."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.979,
      "end": 21.539,
      "text": "Now first,"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.959,
      "end": 26.979,
      "text": "let us convert the speed into meters per second because the time is given in seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.42,
      "end": 33.919,
      "text": "We know speed in meters per second is equal to speed in kilometers per hour into five by eighteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.52,
      "end": 35.36,
      "text": "Putting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.84,
      "end": 39.059,
      "text": "speed is equal to seventy-two into five by eighteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.639,
      "end": 40.86,
      "text": "After simplifying this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.319,
      "end": 43.019,
      "text": "we get twenty meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.52,
      "end": 44.739,
      "text": "Now that we know the speed,"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.34,
      "end": 47.019,
      "text": "we can use the distance formula."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.599,
      "end": 49.819,
      "text": "We know distance is equal to speed into time."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.399,
      "end": 57.219,
      "text": "Since the distance covered to cross the pole is the length of the train, so length of the train is equal to twenty into eighteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.18,
      "end": 65.859,
      "text": "After solving this, we get three hundred sixty meters. So the length of the train is three hundred sixty meters. Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.379,
      "end": 68.819,
      "text": "the correct answer is option C."
    }
  ],
